{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-24641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}\\operatorname{cot}⁡{30}^{∘}-1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-24641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={30}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {30}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({60}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}\\operatorname{cot}⁡{30}^{∘}-1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}}-1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{cos}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}-1}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}-1+{cos}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}-(1-{cos}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing  the Pythagorean identity in the form ${sin}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}=1-{cos}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}-(1-{cos}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}} & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}-{sin}^{2}⁡{30}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘})(\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘})}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘})\\cancel{(\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘})}}{\\cancel{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-24641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "71603e0344de9c030e720c67ee6b94d1321d7bc80f343f0194ae56b9506b558f"} {"question" "q-24641" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-24641" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}-\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{60}^{∘}\\operatorname{sin}⁡{60}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-24641" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{30}^{∘}+\\operatorname{sin}⁡{30}^{∘}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-76641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the exact value of $2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘}).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-76641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={75}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {75}^{∘}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡{150}^{∘} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({75}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({75}^{∘})=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-76641" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "71603e0344de9c030e720c67ee6b94d1321d7bc80f343f0194ae56b9506b558f"} {"question" "q-76641" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-76641" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-76641" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-120029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{100}^{∘}\\operatorname{tan}⁡{50}^{∘}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-120029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={50}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {50}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡({100}^{∘}) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{100}^{∘}\\operatorname{tan}⁡{50}^{∘}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡{50}^{∘}}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}}{2-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2{sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})} \\\\  & =\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing  the Pythagorean identity ${sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}=1-{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{sin}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} & =\\frac{1-{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})}{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})}(1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘})}{\\cancel{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}}} \\\\  & =1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-120029" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "71603e0344de9c030e720c67ee6b94d1321d7bc80f343f0194ae56b9506b558f"} {"question" "q-120029" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-120029" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}"] ["math" "1+{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}"] ["math" "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}-1"] ["math" "{cos}^{2}⁡{50}^{∘}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-120029" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1+\\operatorname{cos}⁡{50}^{∘}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-120088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘})=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-120088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={70}^{∘}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘}) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot {70}^{∘})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) & =2\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({70}^{∘})\\operatorname{cos}⁡({70}^{∘})]\\operatorname{csc}⁡({140}^{∘}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-120088" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "71603e0344de9c030e720c67ee6b94d1321d7bc80f343f0194ae56b9506b558f"} {"question" "q-120088" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-120088" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "1"] ["math" "2"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{csc}⁡({70}^{∘})"] ["math" "2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({140}^{∘})"] ["math" "\\operatorname{csc}⁡({70}^{∘})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-120088" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-120093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-120093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x=\\operatorname{sin}⁡2x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{32}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{32})\n$$\n\nwhich simplifies as\n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}).\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}8\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}) & =4[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{32})]\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}) \\\\  & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the double-angle formula once more with $x=\\frac{\\pi }{16},$ we can further simplify the above expression: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16}) & =2[2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{16})] \\\\  & =2[\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{16})] \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/state.json" "file_sha256" "2134eb7a94c213f9eaf9b3fe71c54bf45a5480886e09a1c0a70d93a2f3a44c40"} {"question" "q-120093" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981249/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "71603e0344de9c030e720c67ee6b94d1321d7bc80f343f